approve":true,"bead_id":"bob-cli-2d.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-2d[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]bob gkeep: drain the Google Keep inbox into Obsidian tasks[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]`bob gkeep` moves every Google Keep inbox note into [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`~/bob/gkeep_inbox.md` as Obsidian tasks and archives each note in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Keep only after its current content is provably in the vault. It [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]also shows Keep and the vault side by side in one reconciliation [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]view, and ships `doctor` and `login` so the setup is diagnosable. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]The output is styled and consistent with `bob plugins`, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]tests never touch live Keep.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bob_gkeep_inbox_drain.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/bob_gkeep_inbox_drain.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-2d[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-2d/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Command skeleton, CLI contract, config, and model[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]skeleton[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]skeleton: register `bob gkeep` and pin the whole CLI surface, including [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]help, typed args, and stub handlers. Add the `gkeep:` config section, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the note model with its canonical content and fingerprint, UI helpers, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the small visibility promotions later phases need.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Embedded Python Keep adapter and Rust adapter client[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]adapter[dim] · [dim][/dim]after skeleton[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adapter: write the pinned PEP 723 gkeepapi adapter (ping, snapshot, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]archive with content guard, exchange) and embed it as a support asset. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Add the Rust client that spawns it under `uv run --script` with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timeout, spinner, and typed errors, plus the shared fake-adapter test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]harness.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Literal renderer, vault ledger, and planner[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after skeleton[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]render: pure, golden-tested note→Markdown rendering with strict [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]escaping. Add the `%%gkeep:v1:…%%` marker format, the vault-wide ledger [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and journal model, the target-note task reader, and the classifier (new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/ pending / revised / skipped) with REF selection.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]login and doctor subcommands[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]auth[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adapter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]auth: implement `bob gkeep login` (hidden cookie prompt or stdin, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exchange, store via `token_store_command`, read-back and reachability [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check) and `bob gkeep doctor` (a styled checklist plus JSON), with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]integration tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]list reconciliation view (default subcommand)[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]list[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adapter, render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]list: implement the two-section Keep/vault reconciliation table with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-note pull states, REF ids, a next-command footer, source filters, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`--all`, graceful Keep failure, and `schema_version: 1` JSON, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]integration tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]pull transaction with guarded archive[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pull[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adapter, render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pull: implement the guarded transaction: snapshot, vault lock, plan, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]compare-and-swap durable write, parse-verify, scoped commit, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]content-guarded archive, journal. Add dry-run Markdown preview, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]human/JSON reports, and crash/conflict integration tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, config seed, and final polish[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after auth, list, pull[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: write `docs/gkeep.md` (the full contract) and the README/doc index[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entries, seed the chezmoi-managed Bob config with a `gkeep:` section, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and do a final consistency pass over help, output, and `just all`.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-2d","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-2d.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},